      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fix language picker localization",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n- Render each language picker option in its own stable/native language, with System and English shown in English.\r\n- Cache localized bundle lookups per language so picker rendering does not repeat filesystem bundle resolution.\r\n- Stop writing explicit app language choices into `AppleLanguages`, and clear stale app-level overrides so System follows macOS language preferences again.\r\n\r\n## Why\r\nUsers can accidentally choose a language they do not understand. The language picker must remain readable enough for them to recover, regardless of the current app language. System should also mean the actual macOS-preferred language, not the last explicit CodexBar language selection.\r\n\r\nRoot cause: explicit language choices were being mirrored into `AppleLanguages`, which could cause System mode to inherit the previous app override. The picker label lookup also bypassed the existing bundle cache when resolving per-language labels.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n- `swift test --filter 'PreferencesPaneSmokeTests|LocalizationBundleCacheTests|LocalizationLanguageCatalogTests'`\r\n- `make check`\r\n- `make test` \r\n\r\n## Screenshot\r\n\r\n| Before | After |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| <img width=\"350\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-04 at 9 01 46 AM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d88c4ca5-2cb0-409d-bdbc-f4427b1f4ac6\" /> | <img width=\"300\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-04 at 10 22 00 AM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/671d5aeb-3404-4ffa-afd5-a54dec9e25b7\" /> |\r\n",
